comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T18:40:36.164Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: introduced typed PmCommandAliasContract metadata with canonical argv, lifecycle, hidden visibility, registration ownership, and migration hints. Seven list aliases are hidden from help/discovery, remain directly executable, emit one stderr hint, and can be suppressed through typed ux.deprecation_hints settings. SDK action compatibility remains available while MCP discovery is canonical. CLI, SDK, MCP, settings, completion, runtime-contract, and parity tests pass."
  "2026-08-17T22:09:23.486Z","harness:codex","Final CodeRabbit round: reconcile the stale blocked_by edge whose chronology conflicts with the feature close and later ADR acceptance; preserve the typed implements relationship."
  "2026-08-17T22:26:36.395Z","harness:codex","Graph correction evidence: removed the stale blocked_by pm-pbyu edge whose timestamp predates later ADR acceptance and contradicted this implemented feature. The typed implements edge remains, preserving architectural provenance without presenting completed historical work as blocked."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T16:23:32.225Z",maintainer-agent,"Scope extension (pm-mpbb ledger lever b, promoted 2026-07-11 when the a22j baseline gate opened): in addition to the once-per-invocation stderr hint in the AC, the mutation/query ENVELOPE must carry the canonical spelling machine-readably when an alias was used (e.g. deprecated_alias + canonical fields), so agents self-migrate programmatically instead of parsing stderr. pm-0mox usage counters are the read side of the same channel. Field naming/placement belongs to the pm-srns uniform envelope spec - coordinate, do not invent a one-off shape here."
